# Yarr Seerr

## Gate

Use when the user asks about Seerr / Overseerr requests, approvals, or
request status via yarr MCP. Skip pure Sonarr/Radarr library edits and
qBit queue work unless the ask chains after a request. Always load
`yarr-safety` for approve/deny/delete writes.

Never invent request id, media id, or user id. Resolve from MCP reads or
user paste.

## Prefer MCP

When a yarr MCP is ready (`user-mcp_yarr`), use tool `seerr` with
actions:

`service_status`, `api_get`, `api_post`, `api_put`, `api_delete`, `help`,
`codemode`, `op`, `snippet_list`, `snippet_save`, `snippet_run`,
`snippet_delete`.

## Read / search

1. `service_status` first when reachability is unclear.
2. Prefer `api_get` / `op` for listing pending or named requests — use
   paths/ops confirmed by `help` or the user; do not invent routes.
3. Report request id, media title, status, requesting user (display name
   only when needed).
4. Paginate with `page` / `page_size` when listing.

## Mutates

Require an explicit verb this turn (`yarr-safety`) for:

- Approving / declining / deleting requests (`api_post` / `api_put` /
  `api_delete` / mutating `op`)
- Creating new requests on someone else's behalf
- Snippet save/run/delete that changes request state

Prefer: confirm media title + request id before approve/deny. Refuse
mass-deny of all pending requests unless the user named that bulk intent.

## Handoff

After approve, downstream *arr/qBit work is a separate surface — only
continue into `yarr-arr` / `yarr-qbit` when the user also asked for grab
or queue follow-up this turn.

## Report shape

- Tool `seerr` + action
- Request id + title + new status
- Note when mutate refused or when follow-up *arr/qBit was skipped

## Out of scope

- Direct Sonarr/Radarr quality profile edits (see `yarr-arr`)
- Plex playback (see `yarr-plex`)
- Hard-coded requester ACLs — resolve from Seerr, not invent

